[question] How can I set up filters on a web browser to prevent sexually explicit content from appearing in search results?
[ground_truth] None
[answer] Answer: I'd be happy to help you block inappropriate content on your screen. Here are some steps you can take:
1.  Use a content filter: Many web browsers, such as Google Chrome and Mozilla Firefox, offer built-in content filters that can block explicit or unwanted content. You can also use third-party extensions or plugins to block specific types of content.
